# Chief of Staff Agent — Cursor Rules

## Start Here

**Always read `MEMORY.md` first.**

**For acceptance criteria (all 23 Key Features):** always read **`docs/ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md`** — canonical wording, AC IDs, rollup, gaps, and per-criterion proof.

**Contributor proof:** `pnpm acceptance` (build + test + file checks). **Executive proof:** `@bigboss` + live APIs — no fixture ingest on product paths.

## Product surface

**Executives use Cursor only** — `@bigboss` in chat or the agent picker. See `README.md` and `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`. Do **not** document `pnpm` commands in user-facing README text.

**Contributors** use `CONTRIBUTING.md` for CLI and CI.

## Hard Rules — Never Violate

1. **No auto-send.** No send/post/create on Gmail, Asana, or any service.
2. **No secrets in code or logs.** Never log tokens or raw email body text.
3. **Vercel AI SDK only** for LLM (`ai` package).
4. **`ownerUserId` filter** on every RAG query.
5. **LangSmith** at every AI entrypoint; `LangSmith.flush()` on exit.
6. **TypeScript only.** Vitest for tests.
7. **No mock/fixture ingest or RAG on product paths.** Mocks only in `__tests__/` with `COS_ALLOW_FIXTURES=true` or `pnpm demo-fixtures` (CI).

## AC-02

Packaged as reusable soofi ecosystem agent: `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` + `agents/bigboss.md`. Optional team-kit plugin is for **contributor build-time** guidance only — operators use `@bigboss` + cos-runtime; team-kit subagents are not runtime workers. See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` § Runtime vs build-time.

Architecture: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`  
Deployment: `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`
